# {{ name }}

{% if is_mlproject %}
{{ name }} is a Chap model in the MLproject format. The image runs it with
`chapkit mlproject run`, which serves it with the chapkit REST API that
chap-core calls.
{% elif is_shell %}
{{ name }} is a chapkit model service. The model is in {{ language }} scripts,
which the service runs for each training and prediction.
{% else %}
{{ name }} is a chapkit model service. The model is in Python, in `main.py`.
{% endif %}

The example model predicts, for each location, the mean of `disease_cases` in
the last `window` periods. Replace it with your model.

## Files

| File | What it holds |
|---|---|
{% if is_mlproject %}
| `MLproject` | The name, the options (`user_options`) and the train and predict commands |
{% else %}
| `main.py` | The options (`{{ class_name }}Config`), the service id and the metadata{% if not is_shell %}, and the model{% endif %} |
{% endif %}
{% if is_shell or is_mlproject %}
| `scripts/{{ train_script }}` | Training: it reads the data and writes the model file |
| `scripts/{{ predict_script }}` | Prediction: it reads the model file and writes `sample_0` for each future row |
{% endif %}
| `Dockerfile` | The image, from `{{ base_image }}` |
{% if has_pyproject %}
| `pyproject.toml` | The Python dependencies |
{% endif %}
| `.github/workflows/publish.yml` | Publishes the image to GHCR on a push to `main` and on a `v*.*.*` tag |

## Build the image

```sh
git init && git add . && git commit -m "feat: first version"
docker build --platform linux/amd64 --build-arg GIT_REVISION=$(git rev-parse HEAD) -t {{ service_id }}:dev .
```

chap-core stores a model only if its image has a git revision, so build from a
commit with `GIT_REVISION`.
{% if amd64_only %}

The base image is about 2 GB, and the first pull can take ten minutes or more.
{% endif %}
{% if not is_mlproject %}

The build installs the dependencies from `uv.lock` if the file is there. Run
`uv lock` to make one, and commit it, so that every build gets the same
versions.
{% endif %}

## Run it

To run the model service alone:

```sh
chap-devops run {{ service_id }}:dev
```

To run it with chap-core, and train and predict through it:

```sh
chap-devops init lab --models none
cd lab
chap-devops models add {{ service_id }}:dev
chap-devops up --wait
chap-devops models test {{ model_id }} --backtest
```

The model registers with chap-core as `{{ service_id }}`. This id is the
{% if is_mlproject %}`name` in `MLproject`{% else %}`id` in `main.py`{% endif %}. If you change it, add the image with
`--service-id` and the new id.
{% if is_mlproject %}

To serve the model from this directory with no build, run
`chap-devops chapkit mlproject run .` here. Ctrl-C stops it.

## Make it a chapkit service

To change the model to a chapkit service with a `main.py`, commit first, then
run this here:

```sh
chap-devops chapkit mlproject migrate . --yes
```

chapkit moves `MLproject` and the files the service does not need to `_old/`.
It finds the scripts that the train and predict commands name, in `scripts/`,
and picks the base image from them.
{% endif %}

## After a change

chap-core stores each version of a model only once. Before you build again,
raise the version: {% if is_mlproject %}`version` in `MLproject`{% else %}`version` in `main.py`{% endif %}. Then commit, build
with the same `docker build` line, and run `chap-devops restart` in the deployment.
`chap-devops models test {{ model_id }} --backtest` creates the configured model
`default` of the new version, or `chap-devops models configs sync` does it without a
test.

## Options

{% if is_mlproject %}
The options are under `user_options` in `MLproject`. The scripts read them
from the file that `--config` names, under `user_option_values`.
{% else %}
The options are the fields of `{{ class_name }}Config` in `main.py`.
{% if is_shell %}
The scripts read them from `config.yml`.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

A configured model in chap-core gives each option a value. It belongs to one
version of the model, so add it again after a new version:

```sh
chap-devops models configs add {{ model_id }} --name long --set window=6
```
